    "title": "docs: add guide on handling false positives",
    "body": "##closes #71 \r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nThis PR adds a dedicated guide on identifying and handling false positives across our tooling setup. Providing clear documentation for these scenarios stabilizes the developer experience and ensures team members can maintain high code quality standards without being blocked by false alarms during Soroban smart contract development.\r\n\r\n## Changes Included\r\n- Added a new guide outlining step-by-step procedures for handling false positives in contract analysis/linting tooling.\r\n- Documented common false alarm patterns, suppressing techniques, and resolution workflows.\r\n- Linked the new guide in relevant repository index/documentation files for easy access.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n- [x] Guide correctly covers resolution strategies for false positives.\r\n- [x] Verified markdown formatting and links locally.\r\n- [x] No regressions introduced into the existing codebase or existing documentation flow.\r\n\r\nCloses #<ISSUE_NUMBER>",
